# Implementation Plan: EcoNet IO Backend Foundation (Architecture Kernel)

Build the foundational **Architecture Kernel** for the EcoNet IO backend strictly following the **EcoNet IO 24-Engine Canon (Revision 2026.4.0-CANONICAL)**.

This milestone establishes the 24-engine module structure, immutable canonical engine registry, shared event/command/query contracts, idempotency infrastructure, audit and governance interfaces, and automated architecture compliance tests—without prematurely implementing external business logic outside canonical boundaries.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Canonical Engine Registry Integrity:**  
> The 24 canonical engines are registered with their exact canonical IDs (`01` through `24`) and names as defined in the Canon. No engine will be renamed, merged, or omitted.
> 
> **Zero Private Cross-Engine Imports:**  
> The architecture strictly enforces that no engine may directly import internal files of another engine. All inter-engine communication will occur via the public interface (`index.js`), the Event Bus, or the Command/Query Bus.
> 
> **Backend vs Automation Team Boundary:**  
> The backend core owns domain state, validation, persistence, and deterministic execution. Background daemons, agentic reasoning loops, and external cron workflows belong to the Automation layer consuming backend contracts.

